date-released: "2026-11-13"
abstract: >-
  FUSE (Future-conditioned Software Evolution) asks whether telling a coding
  agent which requirement comes next, while instructing it to implement only
  the current one, makes its code easier for a fresh agent to extend. This
  development release contains the agent harness of the preliminary study,
  its three authored tasks with hidden test suites, two mined development
  triples from Starlette and Strix, and the identity-premium estimator.
